UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53250846022827
DTSTART:20261016T200000Z
DTEND:20261016T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a discussion of the 2026 One Maryland One Book sele
 ction No Sense in Wishing: Essays on Black Music\, Belonging\, and Baltimo
 re by Lawrence Burney. \n\n \n\nNo Sense in Wishing: Essays on Black Music
 \, Belonging\, and Baltimore by Lawrence Burney is a personal and analytic
 al essay collection that showcases his home city of Baltimore\, music from
  throughout the global Black diaspora\, and the traditions that raised him
 . Each essay tells stories of his formative moments and cultural artifacts
  to tell the story of our region’s cultural scene through his unique poi
 nt-of-view. As one of our contemporary rising cultural critics\, Burney’
 s book aptly captures this year’s theme of Revolution\, Reaction\, and R
 eform.\n\n \n\n To register please call the Pennsylvania Avenue Branch at 
 (410) 396‑0399 or email pnn@prattlibrary.org.
GEO:39.309898;-76.642097
LOCATION:Pennsylvania Avenue
SUMMARY:One Maryland One Book Discussion: No Sense in Wishing
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.prattlibrary.org/event/omob-discussion-2026-
 pnn
CATEGORIES:Book Discussions
CATEGORIES:One Maryland One Book
END:VEVENT
